.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1151 AM PDT Sat Aug 29 2026

VFR prevails this afternoon as moderate onshore winds increase with
a few sites experiencing strong gusts around 20 kt in the late
afternoon. Onshore winds become gentle through the evening into the
overnight hours. The OAK 12Z sounding from this morning measured the
marine layer at a depth of ~1400 ft. An upper level low situated
over our area is expected to deepen the marine layer further. A mix
of IFR to low-end MVFR ceilings return tonight across the terminals
with medium confidence on arrival times and ceiling heights.

Vicinity of SFO...Northwest to westerly moderate winds prevail into
the evening with frequent strong gusts around 20 to 25 kt at SFO.
OAK may experience occasional 20 kt gusts during the afternoon.
Winds ease after sunset into the overnight hours. Relied on
persistence from last night on stratus arrival with medium
confidence for MVFR ceilings. Some model guidance hinted at the
possibility for IFR ceilings similar to last night, but given the
expected deepening of the marine layer, the TAF advertises low-end
MVFR.

SFO Bridge Approach...Occasional strong gusts through the afternoon.
Cloud cover may be patchy overnight, depending on how well organized
the marine layer becomes. Otherwise, similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR through the afternoon with an early
arrival of IFR ceilings around sunset for MRY and after sunset for
SNS. Moderate onshore winds prevail through the day and diminish to
gentle overnight.

